  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with multi-profile + avgpool + PCA (config_002, acc=0.591) is the clear best configuration so far, while image-only with ResNet50 single-profile (config_010, acc=0.208) is very weak. The core question for this multimodal study is whether combining the two modalities yields a benefit over the RNA-only baseline. config_018 (multimodal, multi-profile, PCA, ResNet50, avgpool, concat) directly tests this by pairing the best-known RNA setup with the only image encoder already characterized, using the simplest fusion strategy. If accuracy exceeds 0.591, image contributes complementary signal and justifies exploring better image encoders and fusion strategies; if it falls below, image is currently harmful and the budget should shift toward RNA encoder improvements (scvi, scgpt) or stronger image backbones. This is the highest-information experiment because its outcome determines the entire direction of subsequent experiments in a multimodal study."
}

